1
00:00:03,117 --> 00:00:11,501
Cross-sell & RM Workbench
Turn what the group knows about a client into the next sale — and see how each RM is doing.

2
00:00:11,701 --> 00:00:15,021
The RM's day starts on My Workbench
Her home page: enquiries, next-best actions, reviews, KYC, pipeline and meetings

3
00:00:15,021 --> 00:00:21,021
Sign in as Priya Ramdin — Relationship Manager
Relationship manager — works her own book of clients

4
00:00:21,021 --> 00:00:25,141
Next-best actions waiting for her, and her pipeline by stage
Each viewer sees only their own book

5
00:00:25,141 --> 00:00:31,141
The rules run every night across all clients
Fund holder without a loan → Investment-Backed Loan · borrower → Wealth · corporate → FX hedging · HNW → wealth discovery · FMB 2029 → reinvestment

6
00:00:31,141 --> 00:00:36,421
Open the list of next-best actions
Cross-sell & RM Workbench ▸ Next-Best Actions

7
00:00:36,421 --> 00:00:41,901
Each suggestion: the client, the rule that raised it, the entity and the product
Status Open until the RM decides

8
00:00:41,901 --> 00:00:45,861
Jayesh Coret holds funds above MUR 1 million and has no loan
Suggestion: an Investment-Backed Loan — liquidity without selling her funds

9
00:00:45,861 --> 00:00:51,101
Accept or Dismiss — buttons on the suggestion
She knows the client is planning a purchase: Accept

10
00:00:51,101 --> 00:00:55,141
Accepted: the CRM opens an opportunity for the client
At Identified, owned by Priya

11
00:00:55,141 --> 00:01:00,101
Status: Accepted — opportunity opened
The Accept and Dismiss buttons are gone: the decision is made

12
00:01:00,101 --> 00:01:04,661
The new opportunity is linked to the suggestion
Stage Identified · probability 25% · MUR 1,000,000 placeholder value · owner Priya

13
00:01:07,821 --> 00:01:12,781
Now a suggestion that does not fit: Shamim Noël
Real-estate borrower → Wealth / Money Market

14
00:01:12,781 --> 00:01:19,021
Dismiss asks why
The reason is kept on the suggestion

15
00:01:19,021 --> 00:01:23,101
Dismissed — the rule will not raise it again for this client

16
00:01:23,101 --> 00:01:26,341
Dismissed, with the reason on record
Managers see why suggestions were turned down

17
00:01:26,341 --> 00:01:30,661
Priya meets Jayesh Coret to discuss the loan
Cross-sell & RM Workbench ▸ Meeting Notes ▸ New

18
00:01:30,661 --> 00:01:40,541
A structured note: pick the template — Discovery meeting
Templates: discovery, review, credit visit, call, event follow-up

19
00:01:40,541 --> 00:01:50,141
Objectives, outcomes and next steps
The note appears in Priya's calendar feed, with the follow-up date

20
00:01:50,141 --> 00:01:53,141
Saved — the meeting counts on her workbench and on the RM League Table
Meetings by RM

21
00:01:53,141 --> 00:01:59,341
Put a real value on the opportunity
MUR 6 million, closing in about two months

22
00:01:59,341 --> 00:02:06,941
Value MUR 6,000,000 · probability 25% at Identified
Weighted value = value × probability

23
00:02:06,941 --> 00:02:16,301
The opportunity board: Identified → Qualified → Proposal → Negotiation → Won / Lost
Drag the card as the deal moves on

24
00:02:16,301 --> 00:02:25,941
Qualified: the stage sets the probability to 40%
Weighted value MUR 2,400,000 — the RM can still adjust the probability

25
00:02:25,941 --> 00:02:35,341
Terms sent — Proposal (60%, Best case)
Then Negotiation (80%, Commit)

26
00:02:35,341 --> 00:02:41,581
The client signs — Won
100% · forecast Closed

27
00:02:41,581 --> 00:02:46,861
Won: probability 100%, forecast Closed
Won business is what her quarterly target measures

28
00:02:46,861 --> 00:02:58,381
Arvind Jugnauth · Investment-Backed Loan: the client went elsewhere
Move it to Lost

29
00:02:58,381 --> 00:03:05,261
Blocked: a lost opportunity needs a loss reason
Price, competitor, timing, no need, not eligible — so the losses can be analysed

30
00:03:05,261 --> 00:03:17,261
Loss reason: Competitor
Save, then back to the board

31
00:03:17,261 --> 00:03:20,261
Lost — with its reason, probability 0%
It leaves the open pipeline and the weighted forecast

32
00:03:41,661 --> 00:03:45,141
Each RM has quarterly targets
Cross-sell & RM Workbench ▸ RM Targets & Quotas — set by the managers

33
00:03:45,141 --> 00:03:49,301
New business and revenue targets per quarter, and what was achieved
Attainment % = achieved new business ÷ target

34
00:03:49,301 --> 00:03:52,781
Priya sees her own targets; managers see the whole team
Attainment is recalculated whenever the achieved figures change

35
00:03:52,781 --> 00:03:56,941
The Head of BD follows the whole team
Dashboard ▸ RM League Table

36
00:03:56,941 --> 00:04:04,021
Sign in as Shalini Ramtohul — Head of BD & Strategic Partnerships
Head of BD — sets targets, follows the league table

37
00:04:04,021 --> 00:04:09,301
Meetings and revenue credited, by RM
Activity and results side by side

38
00:04:09,301 --> 00:04:14,821
Open weighted pipeline and won opportunities, by RM
Today's win already counts for Priya

39
00:04:14,821 --> 00:04:19,261
Target attainment by RM
Who is ahead of plan and who needs help

40
00:04:19,341 --> 00:04:27,680
The forecast: every open opportunity with its forecast category and weighted value
Cross-sell & RM Workbench ▸ Opportunities

41
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:35,019
Cross-sell & RM Workbench
The CRM suggests the next sale; the RM decides and works it; managers see the results.
